      "content": "Lift generation is a fascinating interplay between aerodynamics and fundamental physics. Bernoulli's principle describes how the difference in air speed over the curved shape of a wingCreates lower pressure on the top surface than the bottom. This pressure difference, combined with Newton's Third Law, dictates the upward force; the wing pushes air down (downwash), and in reaction, the air pushes the wing up. Thus, the pressure differential explains *why* the forces are unequal, while Newton's Third Law explains the *resultant* upward push.",
