      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Bernoulli's principle fundamentally links the speed of a fluid to its internal energy, or pressure. When air travels faster over the curved top of a wing, its kinetic energy increases, and to conserve the total energy of the system, its potential energy, which we perceive as static pressure, must decrease. Imagine a garden hose: if you restrict the opening (forcing more flow), the speed increases, and if you think about the energy exchange, this heightened velocity corresponds to lower pressure while it's moving rapidly.",
